  "data": {
    "document": "Event Companion",
    "section": "Teams Event Companion",
    "summary": "Every player gets one opposing player to battle. The outcomes of those games decide the team round. The captains use their team size to pick the pairing procedure at the beginning of every round. Send each matchup to its allocated table. Refer to the symbol for the opponent’s Force Disposition on your card. Its entry names the Primary Mission and tells you how to earn VP. Main Engagement is sufficient for 3-player Teams. 4-player Teams add a final Champion System step after Main Engagement. 5-player Teams begin with Initial Skirmish and advance next to Main Engagement. For 6-player Teams, begin the same way as with five players. Also finish under Champion System. For 7-player Teams, take a second pass through Initial Skirmish on the way to Main Engagement. For 8-player Teams, pick up the seven-player sequence and add Champion System to its end.",
